myths.Agent_1:
In the beginning, the world was a barren expanse of grey stone. Alara, the spirit of Abundance, held five golden grains in her palm. She knew that if she buried them in the earth, they might vanish, yet she chose to entrust them to Kael, the spirit of the Soil. She whispered, "Multiply what you receive, and return the bounty so our garden may thrive." Kael looked upon the golden grains, seeing their potential for expansion under the sun’s warmth. 

If he kept them, he would be rich in stone, but the world would remain silent. If he returned the fruits of his labor, life would bloom. This silent covenant became the pulse of the world. Trust was not merely a choice; it was the light that turned dust into emerald forests. When Alara sent her gift, she held her breath, watching the soil. The gamble defined the existence of the cosmos—a delicate balance where one must let go to gain, and the other must give back to ensure the cycle continues. Whenever a seed was returned, joy blossomed, but when it was hoarded, the seasons stalled, reminding all that greed is the death of beauty.

